From: Medvedolog <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] unisocwifi: provide a valid fallback MAC for AP operation

The vendor driver leaves wlan0 at 00:00:00:00:00:00 when neither sunxi
address management, firmware MAC nor a pending address is available.
That is a known UWE5622 quirk and breaks hostapd/AP setup on Orange Pi
Zero 3. A known-working mainline port explicitly requires assigning a
non-zero MAC before starting hostapd.

Generate a locally administered random MAC as the final fallback. The
existing station path stores it in priv->default_mac, so subsequently
created AP interfaces inherit a valid address instead of all zeroes.

Do not add an explicit WIFI_CMD_SET_CHANNEL here: hardware testing showed
that doing so before START_AP triggers the UWE5622 firmware rf_marlin
channel assertion and resets WCN.

--- a/unisocwifi/main.c
+++ b/unisocwifi/main.c
@@ -1091,8 +1091,9 @@ static void sprdwl_set_mac_addr(struct sprdwl_vif *vif, u8 *pending_addr,
 	} else if (priv && is_valid_ether_addr(priv->default_mac)) {
 		ether_addr_copy(addr, priv->default_mac);
 		default_mac_valid = 1;
 	} else {
-		printk("no valid mac address!\n");
+		eth_random_addr(addr);
+		wl_info("no valid mac address, generated fallback %pM\n", addr);
 	}

 	switch (type) {
